          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\n**History of Present Illness:**  \nSeizures began at age 22 years. Epilepsy type remains unknown. The seizures are classified as unknown-onset motor seizures, other type. The reported seizure frequency is approximately 5 per month. The epilepsy is drug-resistant.\n\n**Current Antiseizure Medications:**  \n- Levetiracetam  \n- Topiramate  \n- Brivaracetam  \n\n**Seizure Burden:**  \nApproximately 5 seizures per month despite the current antiseizure medication regimen.\n\n**Assessment:**  \nDrug-resistant epilepsy of unknown type, with unknown-onset motor seizures of other type. The etiology is genetic, associated with a causative KCNQ2 variant, c.881C>T.\n\n**Plan:**  \nCurrent antiseizure medications and seizure frequency were documented. No medication changes or additional interventions are specified.\n\nSincerely,  \nEpilepsy Clinic",
